course: dictionary
lesson: 15508
title: Under the surface
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words are about water, and submerged is one of them. Look at the words around it for clues. «The boat sank, and the rocks were submerged by the rising tide.» The tide is water, and the rocks went under it, so submerged means under water.
explain: Submerged is the past form of the verb submerge, which means to go under water or to push something under water. «The diver submerged the bottle and watched the bubbles rise.» The diver pushed the bottle under the water.
explain: The word can also mean hidden or buried by other things. «The old letter was submerged under a pile of papers.» Nobody can see the letter, just as nobody can see something under water. Try "hidden" in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Submerged means under water or under the surface of a liquid.
fact: Submerge is the verb, and submerges, submerged and submerging are its other forms.
fact: In science, a submerged object pushes water upwards, and this push is called upthrust.
fact: When an object is submerged, the water level rises, and the rise shows how much space the object takes up.
fact: Submerged plants live under water in ponds, and floods can submerge whole towns.
exercise: «The toy boat sank and was submerged.» What does submerged mean? | Shiny and new | Hidden away in a box | Floating high on top | *Under water
exercise: «The stone was partly submerged, so only its top showed above the water.» What does partly submerged mean? | *Under the water for some of its height | Covered with dust | Stuck to the ground | Completely dry
exercise: Which word is the past form of the verb submerge? | submerges | submerging | *submerged
test: «The scientist measured the water rise when the stone was submerged.» What does submerged mean here? | Lifted into the air | *Put under water | Made smaller | Dropped on the floor
test: «His worries were submerged under the noise of the party.» What does submerged suggest? | Washed clean | Shouted loudly | *Hidden or buried, so hard to notice | Made bigger
exam: «Some rocks were partly submerged at low tide.» What does partly submerged mean? | Hidden by the night | *Only some of it is under water | Completely dry | Floating in the air
